{"content_hash": "55deac238622f5aa", "version_id": 128, "article_id": 13, "level_code": "ja_n3", "lang": "ja", "level": 3, "level_label": "N3 中級", "title": "ケイン、イングランド代表125試合の記録を達成　最後のステップは？", "title_zh": "凯恩达成英格兰队125场出场纪录，最后一步还差什么？", "topic": "sports", "source": "skysports", "source_url": "https://www.skysports.com/football/news/12040/13595959/harry-kane-breaks-england-appearance-record-but-can-he-take-that-final-step-to-complete-his-career", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://e0.365dm.com/26/10/1920x1080/skysports-kane-england_7370090.jpg?20261006225617", "credit": ""}, "published_date": "2026-10-06", "word_count": 464, "reading_minutes": 1.5, "lead": "ハリー・ケイン選手がチェコ戦でイングランド代表として125試合目の出場を果たし、ピーター・シルトン氏と並んで歴代最多記録となりました。2ゴール1アシストの活躍でしたが、まだ足りないものがあるようです。", "lead_zh": "哈里·凯恩在对阵捷克的比赛中完成英格兰队第125次出场，追平彼得·希尔顿的队史纪录。他贡献两球一助攻，但似乎还缺少一样东西。", "preview": "ケイン選手は32歳で、21歳のときに代表デビューしました。ウェイン・ルーニー選手やマイケル・オーウェン選手のように10代で注目されたわけではなく、下のリーグから努力して這い上がってきた選手です。そこから11年間で125試合に出場しました。この安定感は本当にすごいことです。", "preview_zh": "凯恩今年32岁，21岁时完成国家队首秀。他并不像韦恩·鲁尼或迈克尔·欧文那样十几岁就备受瞩目，而是从低级别联赛一路努力打拼上来的。此后11年间他出场125次，这种稳定性实在了不起。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 118, "url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@17fa5ff/content/audio/13/ja_n3.mp3", "duration": 98.225, "size_bytes": 593136, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "ja-JP-NanamiNeural", "word_count": 304, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@17fa5ff/content/data/versions/128.json", "paragraphs": ["ケイン選手は32歳で、21歳のときに代表デビューしました。ウェイン・ルーニー選手やマイケル・オーウェン選手のように10代で注目されたわけではなく、下のリーグから努力して這い上がってきた選手です。そこから11年間で125試合に出場しました。この安定感は本当にすごいことです。", "イングランドの最近の公式戦101試合のうち、ケイン選手が出られなかったのは2024年のギリシャ戦だけです。つまり、ほぼすべての試合に出てきたということです。彼は「痛みがあってもプレーしてきた」と話します。けがが多かったルーニー選手と比べると、その差はとても大きいです。", "ケイン選手は「代表のためにすべてを捧げたい」と言います。ロナウド選手がポルトガル代表を離れた同じ日に、彼は記録を作りました。だからこそ、その姿勢が際立ちます。彼は「上にいる時こそ、もっと成長できる」と語り、今も向上心を持ち続けています。", "しかし、彼にはまだ国際大会でのタイトルがありません。1966年以来、イングランドは大きな大会で優勝していないからです。ケイン選手は「記録よりも優勝と交換したい」とまで言います。2028年のユーロ、そして次のワールドカップが最後のチャンスになるかもしれません。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["凯恩今年32岁，21岁时完成国家队首秀。他并不像韦恩·鲁尼或迈克尔·欧文那样十几岁就备受瞩目，而是从低级别联赛一路努力打拼上来的。此后11年间他出场125次，这种稳定性实在了不起。", "在英格兰最近的101场正式比赛中，凯恩只有2024年对阵希腊那场没能出场。也就是说，他几乎参加了所有比赛。他说“即使有伤痛也坚持上场”。与伤病不断的鲁尼相比，差距非常明显。", "凯恩说“愿意为国家队付出一切”。就在C罗离开葡萄牙队的那一天，他创造了纪录。正因如此，他的态度才格外突出。他说“站在顶峰时更要继续成长”，至今仍保持着上进心。", "但他还没有国际大赛的冠军。因为自1966年以来，英格兰从未在大赛中夺冠。凯恩甚至说“愿意用纪录去换冠军”。2028年欧洲杯，以及下一届世界杯，也许是他最后的机会。"], "body": "ケイン選手は32歳で、21歳のときに代表デビューしました。ウェイン・ルーニー選手やマイケル・オーウェン選手のように10代で注目されたわけではなく、下のリーグから努力して這い上がってきた選手です。そこから11年間で125試合に出場しました。この安定感は本当にすごいことです。\n\nイングランドの最近の公式戦101試合のうち、ケイン選手が出られなかったのは2024年のギリシャ戦だけです。つまり、ほぼすべての試合に出てきたということです。彼は「痛みがあってもプレーしてきた」と話します。けがが多かったルーニー選手と比べると、その差はとても大きいです。\n\nケイン選手は「代表のためにすべてを捧げたい」と言います。ロナウド選手がポルトガル代表を離れた同じ日に、彼は記録を作りました。だからこそ、その姿勢が際立ちます。彼は「上にいる時こそ、もっと成長できる」と語り、今も向上心を持ち続けています。\n\nしかし、彼にはまだ国際大会でのタイトルがありません。1966年以来、イングランドは大きな大会で優勝していないからです。ケイン選手は「記録よりも優勝と交換したい」とまで言います。2028年のユーロ、そして次のワールドカップが最後のチャンスになるかもしれません。", "body_zh": "凯恩今年32岁，21岁时完成国家队首秀。他并不像韦恩·鲁尼或迈克尔·欧文那样十几岁就备受瞩目，而是从低级别联赛一路努力打拼上来的。此后11年间他出场125次，这种稳定性实在了不起。\n\n在英格兰最近的101场正式比赛中，凯恩只有2024年对阵希腊那场没能出场。也就是说，他几乎参加了所有比赛。他说“即使有伤痛也坚持上场”。与伤病不断的鲁尼相比，差距非常明显。\n\n凯恩说“愿意为国家队付出一切”。就在C罗离开葡萄牙队的那一天，他创造了纪录。正因如此，他的态度才格外突出。他说“站在顶峰时更要继续成长”，至今仍保持着上进心。\n\n但他还没有国际大赛的冠军。因为自1966年以来，英格兰从未在大赛中夺冠。凯恩甚至说“愿意用纪录去换冠军”。2028年欧洲杯，以及下一届世界杯，也许是他最后的机会。", "text": "ケイン選手は32歳で、21歳のときに代表デビューしました。ウェイン・ルーニー選手やマイケル・オーウェン選手のように10代で注目されたわけではなく、下のリーグから努力して這い上がってきた選手です。そこから11年間で125試合に出場しました。この安定感は本当にすごいことです。 イングランドの最近の公式戦101試合のうち、ケイン選手が出られなかったのは2024年のギリシャ戦だけです。つまり、ほぼすべての試合に出てきたということです。彼は「痛みがあってもプレーしてきた」と話します。けがが多かったルーニー選手と比べると、その差はとても大きいです。 ケイン選手は「代表のためにすべてを捧げたい」と言います。ロナウド選手がポルトガル代表を離れた同じ日に、彼は記録を作りました。だからこそ、その姿勢が際立ちます。彼は「上にいる時こそ、もっと成長できる」と語り、今も向上心を持ち続けています。 しかし、彼にはまだ国際大会でのタイトルがありません。1966年以来、イングランドは大きな大会で優勝していないからです。ケイン選手は「記録よりも優勝と交換したい」とまで言います。2028年のユーロ、そして次のワールドカップが最後のチャンスになるかもしれません。", "vocab": [{"word": "出場", "pos": "noun", "zh": "出场", "note": "スポーツで試合に出ること"}, {"word": "記録", "pos": "noun", "zh": "纪录", "note": "数字や成績を残すこと"}, {"word": "安定感", "pos": "noun", "zh": "稳定性", "note": "いつも同じようにできること"}, {"word": "代表", "pos": "noun", "zh": "代表（国家队）", "note": "国を代表するチーム"}, {"word": "活躍", "pos": "noun", "zh": "活跃、出色表现", "note": "試合でいい働きをすること"}, {"word": "努力", "pos": "noun", "zh": "努力", "note": "がんばること"}, {"word": "姿勢", "pos": "noun", "zh": "态度、姿态", "note": "物事への向き合い方"}, {"word": "向上心", "pos": "noun", "zh": "上进心", "note": "もっとよくなろうとする気持ち"}, {"word": "タイトル", "pos": "noun", "zh": "冠军、头衔", "note": "大会で優勝すること"}, {"word": "優勝", "pos": "noun", "zh": "夺冠", "note": "大会で1位になること"}, {"word": "チャンス", "pos": "noun", "zh": "机会", "note": "いい機会のこと"}, {"word": "語る", "pos": "verb", "zh": "讲述、谈论", "note": "意見や考えを話すこと"}], "title_original": "Kane sums up England legacy on special night - but can he make that final step?", "summary_original": "Some things are inevitable in life. Harry Kane delivering for England is always one of those inevitabilities. On his momentous, milestone match, he stuck to the script perfectly.", "body_original": "Analysis\nHarry Kane breaks England appearance record but can he take that final step to complete his career?\nHarry Kane got two goals and an assist on his 125th cap for England in the 3-0 win over the Czech Republic; the England captain is now level with Peter Shilton at the top of the Three Lions' all-time appearance list - but Kane still needs that trophy to be the undisputed best\nSam Blitz\nFootball Journalist\n@SamBIitz\nTuesday 6 October 2026 23:22, UK\nPlease use Chrome browser for a more accessible video player\nSome things are inevitable in life. Harry Kane delivering for England is always one of those inevitabilities. On his momentous, milestone match, he stuck to the script perfectly.\nOn his 125th cap, Kane did what Kane does best under the Wembley arch - stealing the show, leading the way, winning the game for England.\nEveryone knew he would score in this match. It's the same feeling you get in\nevery\nmatch. But he still gets the buzz.\nEngland 3-0 Czech Republic - report and reaction\nWho are the winners and losers of this England camp?\n\"I think this is even beyond my wildest dreams,\" he said after the game. \"To be now at 125, it's just an extreme privilege.\"\nThis match - and the three goals he contributed to England's cause on his special night - was a perfect summary of Harry Kane's England career.\nThe first goal saw him venture out to the right wing, highlighting Kane's ability to pop up anywhere on the pitch. Quarterback, out wide, it doesn't matter. It's classic Kane.\nBut his two goals were classic centre-forward strikes. Right in the heart of the penalty area, almost a throwback to the classic No 9.\n\"He's playing at a level that is unmatched,\" said Jude Bellingham on Kane's record-breaking night. \"He's scoring goals for fun, he's dropping deep and playing passes in behind and contributing, making tackles and everything. He's only getting better.\"\nWhat makes Kane's achievement even more incredible is he has reached 125 caps despite making his England debut at 21. For a generational talent in the modern game, that's somewhat rare. Bellingham, for example, was 17 when he played his first game.\nKane did not have the teenage sensation moment Wayne Rooney or Micheal Owen had. Bukayo Saka and Rio Ferdinand were also 19 on their England debuts. Declan Rice and Phil Foden were 20. Kane was the slow starter who forged his way up through the EFL and became a national hero.\nMonterosa\nThis content is provided by\nMonterosa\n, which may be using cookies and other technologies.\nTo show you this content, we need your permission to use cookies.\nYou can use the buttons below to amend your preferences to enable\nMonterosa\ncookies or to allow those cookies just once.\nYou can change your settings at any time via the\nPrivacy Options\n.\nUnfortunately we have been unable to verify if you have consented to\nMonterosa\ncookies.\nTo view this content you can use the button below to allow\nMonterosa\ncookies for this session only.\nEnable Cookies\nAllow Cookies Once\nAnd what has followed is 125 caps in 11 years. The remarkable consistency is summarised by his availability. He's always there for England.\nIn England's last 101 competitive matches - which spans a decade - Kane has been available for selection for all but one of them: the Nations League loss to Greece in 2024.\nEvery single other game, he has been able to be called upon for the Three Lions. A century of near-perfectly consistent England performances over the span of a decade.\n\"For sure there's times I've played through the pain\", he said. \"I think every player at some stage plays through the pain or niggles or some sort of injury.\n\"I think the last six years or so I've been extremely consistent in that sense and been available. I think availability is one of the biggest strengths you can have at this level.\"\nNow it's important to recognise that Kane hasn't always been 100 per cent fit in those 100 matches. The Euro 2024 campaign and final spring to mind where he was clearly carrying something but playing through the pain.\nBut his predecessor at the England elite level in Rooney was riddled with injury sagas through his career - Euro 2004 and the 2006 World Cup especially.\nThe main image of his 2010 World Cup highlight reel was him shouting down the TV cameras to England fans, then he faded out of form in 2012, 2014 and 2016 - to the point where he was no longer the main man. Kane has shown the consistency Rooney never could.\nNow Rooney, Owen and Co were part of a different generation where playing for England was not as attractive as it is now. Turning up regularly for international duty was not as common, with the 'club first culture' well-documented on many levels.\nBut then again, Kane's big night came on the same evening that Cristiano Ronaldo revealed his reasons for leaving the Portugal camp. Even the very best can easily turn away from the national team for any reason. Kane has never even given a glimmer of that attitude in his 11 years.\n\"To reach the highest level on a consistent basis you've always got to be hungry, you've always got to be striving for more,\" he said.\n\"I think sometimes players or people can reach the top and think it's time to take their foot off the gas and that's when you see players maybe fall.\n\"For me it's the opposite. When I'm at the top it's to do even more, find even more improvement. That's what I'm doing right now.\"\nKane is the exemplary player England needed for this generation - but all that remains is for him to confirm his place as the greatest player in\nany\ngeneration.\nIs he already England's best? Quite possibly. Record appearance maker and goalscorer is hard to top and argue against. But the one thing Ronaldo, Bobby Charlton and Bobby Moore have over him is silverware at international level. \"For sure I'd swap all [the caps and goals] to win something with England.\"\nBut Kane also said: \"Every player has a ceiling.\" What is his? Has he already reached it? \"I hope not. I hope there's still more to go. I guess only time dictates that, where everyone's ceiling is.\n\"Right now I still feel like I've got room to improve. I just said that I've come off the back of my best season ever at 32 years old and right now I feel even in a better place.\"\nThere is still plenty for him to get. Kane is first eyeing up 100 goals at international level, joining a very elite club of strikers to manage that feat. He will surely get there.\n\"I try not to think about it too much,\" he said, with a sense of humility. \"It's like being a cricketer in the 90s, the more you think about the 100, you don't know where to get there.\nBut in this all-time great innings - as well as the upcoming Ballon D'Or trophy, which he surely has more than half a chance for - delivering a first major international trophy since 1966 is the ultimate prize.\nKane has at least one more bite at the trophy cherry. He looks set to appear at Euro 2028 and possibly he can squeeze out one last crack at the World Cup, following this summer's disappointment.\n\"I'm in great shape,\" he said. \"Some of the players I've played with went into their late 30s and are still at the highest level and are even in their 40s now. It's season by season with me.\n\"As long as I feel like I can help the team and be valuable for the team I'll be around. At the moment I feel like I can't help the team, I won't and that's the way I am. We'll have to see.\"\nFor now, one message stands with Kane. \"Don't give yourself any regrets.\" He has done so much - but it's time for the last, big challenge. Win it all. Win what remains.\nAround Sky\nUpgrade to get all of Sky Sports, including 1500 live football matches this season\nNot got Sky? Get instant access to Sky Sports with no contract", "fetched_at": "2026-10-07T00:54:02.318992", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "ケイン", "s": 0.125, "e": 0.463, "sm": 125, "em": 462, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "選手", "s": 0.475, "e": 0.9, "sm": 475, "em": 899, "cs": 3, "ce": 5, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "は", "s": 0.912, "e": 1.062, "sm": 912, "em": 1062, "cs": 5, "ce": 6, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "32", "s": 1.087, "e": 1.704, "sm": 1087, "em": 1704, "cs": 6, "ce": 8, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "歳", "s": 1.704, "e": 2.013, "sm": 1704, "em": 2012, "cs": 8, "ce": 9, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "で", "s": 2.025, "e": 2.2, "sm": 2025, "em": 2199, "cs": 9, "ce": 10, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "、", "s": 2.2, "e": 2.562, "sm": 2199, "em": 2562, "cs": 10, "ce": 11, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "21", "s": 2.562, "e": 3.096, "sm": 2562, "em": 3095, "cs": 11, "ce": 13, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "歳", "s": 3.096, "e": 3.362, "sm": 3095, "em": 3362, "cs": 13, "ce": 14, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "の", "s": 3.375, "e": 3.475, "sm": 3375, "em": 3475, "cs": 14, "ce": 15, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "とき", "s": 3.487, "e": 3.737, "sm": 3487, "em": 3737, "cs": 15, "ce": 17, "si": 0}, {"i": 11, "w": "に", "s": 3.75, "e": 3.9, "sm": 3750, "em": 3900, "cs": 17, "ce": 18, "s